	title="Therapists Program"
	description="A three-year therapist training program at the Desert Mindfulness Center."
>
	<p>
		A three-year therapist training program run by the Desert Mindfulness Center, active since
		2011. The curriculum combines Buddhist-inspired experiential psychotherapy with theoretical
		study, practical application, and clinical training in mindfulness-based approaches.
	</p>
	<h2>Program structure</h2>
	<ul>
		<li>One weekly study day (Wednesdays) plus intensive retreat periods</li>
		<li>Location: Kibbutz Hatzerim, in a comfortable, well-ventilated hall</li>
		<li>In-person attendance required; Zoom participation available in special cases</li>
	</ul>
	<h2>Teaching philosophy</h2>
	<p>
		"The central therapeutic tool is therapeutic presence" — from which the clinical practices
		grow. Training includes several retreats to deepen learning and develop qualities of
		acceptance, presence, and compassion.
	</p>
	<h2>Faculty</h2>
	<p>
		Led by Dr. Oded Arbel (psychiatrist and program director), alongside prominent teachers in
		Buddhist studies, somatic psychology, and meditation practice from Israel's academic and
		therapeutic communities.
	</p>
	<h2>Who it's for</h2>
	<p>
		Mental-health professionals — psychologists, psychiatrists, social workers, physicians, and
		creative-arts therapists — with prior psychodynamic training. Admission requires a personal
		interview.
	</p>
	<h2>Annual cost</h2>
	<ul>
		<li>Three-year program: 8,000 NIS per year</li>
		<li>Graduate continuation program: 4,500 NIS per year</li>
	</ul>
	<h2>Registration</h2>
	<p>Registration is via an online form; enrollment is limited.</p>
</ProsePage>
